#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_even

#% text
# `is_even(n)` gives `true` when `n` is an even integer, else `false`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Anything that is not an explicit integer gives `false`: a symbol, a closed form such as `2*pi`, a machine real such as `2.0`, a string. This is the rule of `is_integer` and `is_prime`, so `is_even` can always be used as a test in `select` or `count_if`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_even(4)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_even(7)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_even(-10)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Big integers:

#% cell
is_even(2^200)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# Select the even elements of a list:

#% cell
select(range(10), is_even)
#% output
#= [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A machine real is not an integer, even when it has no fractional part:

#% cell
is_even(2.0)
#% output
#= false

#% text
# Use `is_integer` first, or `round`, when the argument may be a real:

#% cell
is_even(round(2.0))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_odd`, `mod`, `is_integer`, `select`
